lil agents for Windows
======================

This project is a Windows port of "lil agents" by Ryan Stephen:

    https://github.com/ryanstephen/lil-agents

The original is a macOS application written in Swift/AppKit and licensed under the MIT
License, Copyright (c) 2026 Ryan Stephen. That license and copyright notice are retained
in full in the LICENSE file of this repository and apply to this derivative work.

What is derived from the original
---------------------------------

* The application design: two characters walking on the dock/taskbar, click-to-open
  themed popover terminals, provider switching, thinking bubbles.
* The walk timing constants, movement curve, and per-character tuning values, which were
  derived by the original author from frame-by-frame analysis of the walk animations.
* The four colour themes (Peach, Midnight, Cloud, Moss), ported value-for-value.
* The thinking and completion phrase lists.
* The agent session protocol design and the per-provider CLI event parsing.

Artwork and audio
-----------------

The character animations for Bruce and Jazz, and the completion sound effects, are the
original author's work. The sprite frames in src/LilAgents/Assets/sprites were produced
by transcoding the original transparent HEVC videos (walk-bruce-01.mov, walk-jazz-01.mov)
to per-frame PNGs with an alpha channel, because no Windows media stack decodes HEVC's
alpha auxiliary layer. They are the same artwork in a different container.

What is new in this port
------------------------

All Windows platform code, written from scratch: taskbar geometry via SHAppBarMessage,
layered-window management, WM_NCHITTEST alpha hit testing, per-monitor DPI handling,
sprite animation and caching, the .cmd shim resolution layer, UTF-8 stream pumping,
settings persistence, the tray menu, and the WPF UI.
